206
00:22:27,840 --> 00:22:33,320
the LED may turn on and off three or four times.
This is called bouncing.

207
00:22:33,320 --> 00:22:39,279
We can also eliminate bouncing in hardware
by designing a suitable RC circuit,

208
00:22:39,279 --> 00:22:44,159
but that requires more components
and makes the circuit more complicated.

209
00:22:44,159 --> 00:22:50,960
We can also handle it in software.
In a separate session, I have written the code

210
00:22:50,960 --> 00:22:57,520
to completely debounce the push button,
and this is used in many applications.

211
00:22:57,520 --> 00:23:01,200
This is the debounce
method.

212
00:23:01,200 --> 00:23:07,799
As for the hardware connections,
I explained them fully in the previous diagram.

213
00:23:07,799 --> 00:23:13,240
I showed you how to connect the LED,
how to connect the interrupt pin,

214
00:23:13,240 --> 00:23:17,559
and why a resistor is needed
to limit the current.

215
00:23:17,559 --> 00:23:23,760
The grounds should also be common.
Keep in mind that the Blue Pill ground

216
00:23:23,760 --> 00:23:29,559
and the LED ground must be connected together.
There is nothing else special here.

217
00:23:29,559 --> 00:23:39,240
We have now run the program completely
and everything worked without errors.

218
00:23:39,240 --> 00:23:47,279
Now we want to load the program
onto the microcontroller.

219
00:23:47,279 --> 00:23:53,520
We load the program here
so that it is completely transferred.

220
00:23:53,520 --> 00:24:01,039
After the program has been loaded onto
the microcontroller, we press the reset switch

221
00:24:01,039 --> 00:24:06,640
on the Blue Pill.
And here, as you can see,

222
00:24:06,640 --> 00:24:11,080
it turns on once and off once.
That brief change is because of

223
00:24:11,080 --> 00:24:18,840
the same debounce issue.
The wiring is also exactly as I explained.

224
00:24:18,840 --> 00:24:26,279
Here we have PA0,
which is connected with this yellow wire

225
00:24:26,279 --> 00:24:32,760
to the push button.
The other side of the push button

226
00:24:32,760 --> 00:24:37,919
is connected to 3.3 volts.
PA3 is also connected

227
00:24:37,919 --> 00:24:44,279
through a 1-kiloohm resistor to the LED.
The positive lead is connected to PA3,

228
00:24:44,279 --> 00:24:49,799
and the negative lead is connected to ground.
Now, by pressing the push button,

229
00:24:49,799 --> 00:24:57,200
the LED turns on once. Again, there is the
debounce issue, but once we handle it,

230
00:24:57,200 --> 00:25:00,200
it will turn on and off once per press.
Thank you, and may God protect you.
